{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/689173-exigents-great-forks","id":689173,"title":"Exigents & Great Forks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-04T20:57:30-07:00","id":689173,"title":"Exigents & Great Forks","content":"Is it just me or does the inclusion of Exigents in 3rd Ed make you think that Great Forks will have a much greater power base than in previous editions. Not only spiritual/religious power but also the raw military &amp; magical power of having dozens of <u><i>kinds</i></u> of exalted at their disposal. Before they had godblooded to bolster their military but with the extigents I expect that they will be far more mighty in nigh every way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6473-raemus","name":"Raemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T21:01:59-07:00","id":689242,"title":"","content":"I don't think that Great Forks will have &quot;dozens of kinds of Exalted at their disposal.&quot; At least not at first, at least not by default. Remember that the Exigence is seldom granted in even the First Age, and only now are they making a resurgence. John said it's doubtful if there have ever been more than 300 in existence at any time, and that's keeping in mind all Creation and Yu-Shan and stranger realms still.<br /> <br /> I <i>do</i> think folks will flock there as their ranks swell across Creation, including Exigents who feel a need for a spiritual patron or divine ally and such, but it's not gonna be the state of things at the onset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-05-2015, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T21:03:48-07:00","id":689245,"title":"","content":"I imagine it'll make a small difference, but not a massive one. The reason is this:<br /> <br /> Making an Exigent lessens a God. It can even kill weaker gods. This is why there's never been that many, even though most Gods can technically make them. It's something you only make when you're truly desperate. Perhaps you're on the borders of Creation and Fair Folk are about to attack. Perhaps you are God of a city about to be destroyed by a barbarian horde.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if you live in Great Forks, have loads of worshippers, attend parties with other Gods, and so on, why would you want to lessen yourself to create a champion who you may not be able to control?<br /> <br /> Now, I imagine with so many Gods in Great Forks, there'll probably be 2 or 3 Exigents there, but I don't imagine there will be huge numbers of them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T22:10:32-07:00","id":689304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/689173-exigents-great-forks?p=689245#post689245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making an Exigent lessens a God. It can even kill weaker gods. This is why there's never been that many, even though most Gods can technically make them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That and the need to petition the Unconquered Sun for aid and convince him that you deserve to create an Exalted champion, which hasn't been described as an easy process of sending in some paperwork and getting your Exigence within two to three working weeks as long as the criminal record section is empty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T22:13:22-07:00","id":689305,"title":"","content":"I expect that Sol can give you your exigence that day. If it took too much time, Ten Sheaves would be sitting outside the Jade Pleasure Doom with his ticket while the Fair Folk rampaged through that town.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T23:33:17-07:00","id":689368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/689173-exigents-great-forks?p=689305#post689305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I expect that Sol can give you your exigence that day. If it took too much time, Ten Sheaves would be sitting outside the Jade Pleasure Doom with his ticket while the Fair Folk rampaged through that town.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed - when Sol is paying attention to Creation it is possible for him to respond to a god's prayer to him with the Exigence. The term itself means &quot;urgent need&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T23:40:36-07:00","id":689375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/689173-exigents-great-forks#post689173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me or does the inclusion of Exigents in 3rd Ed make you think that Great Forks will have a much greater power base than in previous editions. Not only spiritual/religious power but also the raw military &amp; magical power of having dozens of <u><i>kinds</i></u> of exalted at their disposal. Before they had godblooded to bolster their military but with the extigents I expect that they will be far more mighty in nigh every way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think &quot;at their disposal&quot; is overstating it. It's been mentioned by the writers that Great Forks is something of a hub for the Exigents, and that is a bit of its setting niche in Third Edition, yes. However, they don't inherently serve the state. It's a place many of them (relative to their number) make pilgrimage to where they're collectively elevated above the Dragon-Blooded (individually that may be the case for them in their home culture if the god that Exalted them is a big deal there, like a Chosen of Ahlat in Harborhead, but the impression I have is that Great Forks given its religiously polyglot nature, elevates the Exigents as a rule as an extension of being Hundred God Heresy palooza). That doesn't mean Great Forks can field them as an army. They're all diverse (to the extreme!) free agents.<br /> <br /> There's still only one state in the River Province that can field an army of Exalted.<br /> <br /> But I agree that it does up Great Forks' political position relative to their position in previous editions, or at least better justifies it. It's a definite factor in considering them a major power in the Confederation of Rivers, even if not quite on par with the military and economic centers of Lookshy and Nexus (respectively).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-05-2015, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T22:33:42-07:00","id":690912,"title":"","content":"What about the so-called &quot;dirty bomb&quot; Exalted? Did we ever get any more info on what they're about?<br /> <br /> IIRC, these were &quot;unformatted&quot; exaltations that multiple gods stole and passed around, trading or possibly buying/selling, until they were &quot;imprinted&quot; with the power of many different gods, before finally being used to exalt a mortal.<br /> <br /> I could easily see GF being a hub of this sort of underground dealing/trading in exaltations...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T22:48:50-07:00","id":690918,"title":"","content":"Great Forks probably is the best place for corrupt Gods to do dirty business, as there are plenty of Gods around with little celestial oversight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T04:40:48-07:00","id":691035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/689173-exigents-great-forks?p=690912#post690912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the so-called &amp;quot;dirty bomb&amp;quot; Exalted? Did we ever get any more info on what they're about?<br /> <br /> IIRC, these were &amp;quot;unformatted&amp;quot; exaltations that multiple gods stole and passed around, trading or possibly buying/selling, until they were &amp;quot;imprinted&amp;quot; with the power of many different gods, before finally being used to exalt a mortal.<br /> <br /> I could easily see GF being a hub of this sort of underground dealing/trading in exaltations...</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually figured that happened more in Yu-Shan. <br /> <br /> Also I don't think it's so much a blank Exaltation as a container of divine fire that's designed to have one &quot;flavor&quot; imprinted on it, but can accept many.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T06:55:06-07:00","id":691198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/689173-exigents-great-forks?p=689245#post689245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making an Exigent lessens a God. It can even kill weaker gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we actually know this for sure?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you're wrong, but &quot;empowering the Exigence can kill you&quot; doesn't necessarily completely overlap with &quot;and it lessens you no matter what.&quot;<br /> <br /> It might be more like giving blood. Theoretically, it's possible to suck enough blood out of someone during that procedure to kill them. In practice, they draw enough to be useful, and you're woozy for awhile, but then you recover.<br /> <br /> It could be that if you clear the threshold for empowering an Exigent, doing so leaves you weak for a time, but then your divine essence replenishes itself. It's only if you're so weak that every ounce of your strength needs to go into the Exigence that you cease to be. It isn't like the Incarnae grew appreciably weaker for empowering the &quot;regular&quot; Exaltations, after all.<br /> <br /> Note: this is pure speculation on my part and it might be that we do in fact know making an Exigent permanently weakens a god and I just don't know where to look.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T07:10:12-07:00","id":691211,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure Ten Sheaves was destroyed in the process of Exalting Janest. Granted he was a relatively weak god to begin with. So if there's precedent for destruction then permanent weakening at best isn't unreasonable. <br /> <br /> Also, we don't know if empowering the Celestial Exaltations weakened the Incarnae (maybe? But it's irrelevant in the end). What can be said is the Incarnae are an entirely different order of gods even compared to those right below them in power and station, so comparison may not be helpful. <br /> <br /> Amount of diminishment may also relate to the ultimate power level of the Exalt, but that's just speculation. And probably wouldn't be a good thing if it were a thing because most people would just say &quot;my patron was destroyed and I'm more powerful as a result&quot; and nobody wants that to be a common or optimal thing.<br /> <br /> The Exigence seems narratively framed as an intentional hard choice: the power to call up a superior champion at the risk of your existence. I find that to be much more meaningful than if there's no real risk for most gods to do so. Without risk it's hard to explain why there weren't more Exigents in history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T07:34:42-07:00","id":691241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Why didn\u2019t the Yozis just make their own Exalts?</b><br /> Firstly, the secret was not known to them. Also, the gods and the Chosen did much to keep the knowledge from them. But they knew, even as they worked to deny the Demon Princes this knowledge, that the Yozis were watching, and by observation alone might decipher the secrets of Second Breath. So Autochthon secreted into the notice of She Who Lives in Her Name the knowledge of <b>the Law of Diminishment</b>, which was discovered by the gods when they made their Chosen, and which revealed <b>the wasting away of those who take from themselves to make champions</b>. Seeing Autochthon\u2019s rapid deterioration, and the first setting of the Unconquered Sun, the Masters of Creation were horrified by the notion, and sought other methods by which to gain the advantage. </div> </div> </div>From the Kickstarter's Infernal preview; emphasis mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T07:40:23-07:00","id":691247,"title":"","content":"The Infernals preview mentioned something called the Law of Diminishment - making their Exaltations cost the gods. The Unconquered Sun set for the first time after creating the Solar Exalted. <br /> <br /> Also, from the What We Know wiki:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Q: Are any little gods able to exalt more than one Exigent at once without dying or being weakened to the point of near-nonexistence? (Erinys)<br /> A: Yes, but they must be very mighty. There are several gods who have made Exigents without dying. (John M\u00f8rke) </div> </div> </div>Conclusion: Exaltation is a costly choice. It's less like giving blood and more like a risky organ donation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T07:49:52-07:00","id":691265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/689173-exigents-great-forks?p=691241#post691241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the Kickstarter's Infernal preview; emphasis mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>... ah! I'd completely 100% forgotten all about this. If I ever knew it. I think I did, but am not sure.<br /> <br /> That's some interesting stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T09:05:40-07:00","id":691328,"title":"","content":"I imagine the greatest benefit to Great Forks will be all the mortals who are so competent in their chosen field that they can plausibly ask the gods for Exaltation. It wouldn't be enough to compete with Lookshy's Dragon-Blooded, but it's still be pretty damn impressive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T12:27:04-07:00","id":691582,"title":"","content":"Great Forks has been a bit of a hub for powerful characters in previous editions. Black and White Treatise mentions that there is a Lunar Celestial Sorcerer who maintains a sorcerous lodge there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T15:05:39-07:00","id":691745,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that a major thing with GF is that it still hasn't recovered from losing a massive number of troops, which likely included some of their most powerful citizens. Frankly, I doubt Exigents would be normally created and enlisted in a normal army, esp with Exigence being so rare until recently. Now, however, with it flaring up into active use *and* a desperate need for powerful soldiers, the City of Temples may start seeing a lot more of them, used to supplement the God-Blooded police and military...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T15:51:27-07:00","id":691763,"title":"","content":"I wonder how much care Celestial Exalts need to have in Great Forks this time around. In 2e the general law was &quot;Celestials of any sort are allowed to settle and even work for the Three, but break the laws and we break your face&quot;. Personally I liked that and hope that's still the general stance, but with Lookshy being back to its old stance on the Anathema one can see a plausible argument for its approach filtering down to other city-states. Especially given that staying in Lookshy's good graces is rather important for national security.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T16:48:23-07:00","id":691790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CycloneJoker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/689173-exigents-great-forks?p=691763#post691763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">with Lookshy being back to its old stance on the Anathema</div> </div> </div> </div>Lookshy's stance on Anathema never changed. Karal Linwei just personally didn't want to kill Fire Orchid and hid the fact that she was an Anathema from the rest of the nation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T22:45:52-07:00","id":695731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/689173-exigents-great-forks?p=691790#post691790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lookshy's stance on Anathema never changed. Karal Linwei just personally didn't want to kill Fire Orchid and hid the fact that she was an Anathema from the rest of the nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, in 2e Lookshy didn't give as much of a damn. They weren't exactly FRIENDLY towards Celestials but they wouldn't kill them absent a good solid reason. Which I suppose isn't that different depending on how you look at things; it just changes what the definition of a &quot;good solid reason&quot; is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T23:17:23-07:00","id":695765,"title":"","content":"The thing to remember with Lookshy is not that the Immaculate Faith is lighter on Crlestials than the Immaculate Order - in principle it isn't.<br /> <br /> The difference is that the Immaculate Faith by comparison isn't proselytizing outside the Legion, and Lookshy doesn't dominate the rest of the River Province like it's their personal satrapies to enforce their ideology within. That said, they're going to regard any Solars, Lunars, or Abyssal Exalted as potential threats to the peace, order, and independence of the River Province first and foremost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T23:41:35-07:00","id":695775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/689173-exigents-great-forks?p=695765#post695765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing to remember with Lookshy is not that the Immaculate Faith is lighter on Crlestials than the Immaculate Order - in principle it isn't.<br /> <br /> The difference is that the Immaculate Faith by comparison isn't proselytizing outside the Legion, and Lookshy doesn't dominate the rest of the River Province like it's their personal satrapies to enforce their ideology within. That said, they're going to regard any Solars, Lunars, or Abyssal Exalted as potential threats to the peace, order, and independence of the River Province first and foremost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well now, apparently, Lookshy is capable of running its own Wyld Hunts that I presume can range aaaaall over the River Province and maybe a wee bit beyond in some directions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T00:06:47-07:00","id":695809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CycloneJoker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/689173-exigents-great-forks?p=695775#post695775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well now, apparently, Lookshy is capable of running its own Wyld Hunts that I presume can range aaaaall over the River Province and maybe a wee bit beyond in some directions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I didn't know they had their own Wyld Hunt. Is that something the writers have confirmed for 3rd Edition? I missed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T01:22:17-07:00","id":695847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/689173-exigents-great-forks?p=695809#post695809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I didn't know they had their own Wyld Hunt. Is that something the writers have confirmed for 3rd Edition? I missed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, lemme go get the bit that talks about it...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-exalted-3rd-edition/posts/733062\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...n/posts/733062</a><br /> <br /> Second to last paragraph of the previewed text here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T01:57:55-07:00","id":695853,"title":"","content":"I think they had the Wyld Hunt in 1e, they just didn't do it that often.<br /> I'd imagine the difference between the Realm and Lookshy's Wyld Hunt is that the Realm hunt and kill Anathema wherever they can find them (if it's in their sphere of influence and is thus feasible, at least), whereas Lookshy only brings it out against Anathema that are actively causing problems. Plus, their military mind-set probably makes it more of a case of tabulating projected losses vs projected benefits, rather than announcing that it's absolutely the duty of the Dragonblood to slay Anathema, and they should be willing to die for that if necessary. More special ops and less Crusade. \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T02:42:20-07:00","id":695904,"title":"","content":"The difference is that the Realm runs Wyld Hunts while Lookshy is a place that Wyld Hunts come from. I do believe they will be writing it that Lookshy will be pretty damn earnest about Anathema going away, just that it's a duty that certain heroes are expected to take up for themselves, rather than something directly managed by the government.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T02:49:48-07:00","id":695907,"title":"","content":"I didn't imagine Lookshyan Dragon-Blooded had enough freedom to go off on personal glory-hunting adventures like that. Aren't they universally career military?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T02:54:14-07:00","id":695909,"title":"","content":"Possibly. That would make it deniable from a diplomatic stand-point as well.<br /> <br /> The 7th Legion probably does occasionally try to kill Anathema who are a direct threat to the Scavenger Lands, and they might even call it a Wyld Hunt (for propaganda purposes), but in the same way they do black ops missions anyway.<br /> It's imp\u200bortant to remember that the Wyld Hunt is not purely about murdering people just because they glow out of their head: the Solars and Lunars are, absolutely, a threat to the established powers of Creation. Lookshy may not be chomping at the bit to murder every Solar they can find, but that doesn't mean they want to see a circle of Solars conquer all the Scavenger Lands (just like they don't want barbarians or the Realm doing it), and so if Harmonious Doctor of Peace goes around curing the plague in Nexus, they'll do nothing, but if Iron Warlord of Conquest forces all the Hundred Kingdoms to unite under his banner, I imagine sending a &quot;Wyld Hunt&quot; to kill him is very likely. Though this is going to be more a matter of commandos who try poisoning him first and then snipe him if that fails, than kung-fu Monks challenging him to face them, just because this is the mentality of Lookshy.<br /> <br /> I also imagine, as Looksh\u200by hires out mercenaries to other River Pronvince kingdoms all the time, these mercenaries would be even more in demand when it's time to fight an Anathema warlord compared to a regular barbarian warlord, because who's going to know more about killing Anathema than Lookshy? Not like anyone's going to want to ask the Realm for help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-10-2015, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T02:55:44-07:00","id":695911,"title":"","content":"I think sacred pilgrimages to destroy demon creatures who threaten the perfected hierarchy and the dominance of the Dragon Blooded can provide a bit of special dispensation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T05:20:39-07:00","id":695980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/689173-exigents-great-forks?p=695911#post695911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think sacred pilgrimages to destroy demon creatures who threaten the perfected hierarchy and the dominance of the Dragon Blooded can provide a bit of special dispensation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably. Depends how strapped for cash Lookshy is, which political faction the local commander is a member of, how dangerous it looks, and how expensive it's likely to be. They might just charge cost or say they'll do it but demand help from locals.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T06:42:37-07:00","id":696015,"title":"","content":"I imagine Lookshy tends to be content with driving the Anathema away as opposed solely to killing them like the Realm. Basically if an Anathema is willing to leave the Scavenger Lands and doesn't pose a direct threat, then Lookshy is willing to let them go. They just don't have the Realm's manpower or resources so they have to have a slightly more reasonable stance when dealing with Anathema. So they may sometimes be more willing to look the other way if a Solar is &quot;just passing through&quot; whereas you could never expect similar treatment from the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T09:17:31-07:00","id":696166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/689173-exigents-great-forks?p=696015#post696015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine Lookshy tends to be content with driving the Anathema away as opposed solely to killing them like the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good idea! Let the dangerously powerful person escape by the skin of their teeth after forming up as a zealous murder-posse! That's sure to not make an enemy of someone who could return for revenge years or even generations later at the head of a conquering army, after you assaulted and drove them out of their homelands for the crime of existing! <br /> <br /> Generally speaking, if the situation calls for a Wyld Hunt being assembled in the first place, the situation calls for the target being <i>dead</i>, not displaced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T11:22:57-07:00","id":696300,"title":"","content":"One of the big differences between the Realm and Lookshy is that Lookshy is merely a regional power and lacks a lot of the wealth, manpower, Exalted and supernatural backing that the Realm possesses. There are probably occasions where Lookshy decides it simply isn't worth it to expend the lives of their soldiers and their arsenal of artifacts, or send those soldiers on extended hunts halfway across the world for months or years, if the Anathema is clearly more interested in going somewhere else than in staying in the Scavenger Lands.<br /> <br /> So while in theory, Lookshy's Wild Hunt is every bit as dangerous and tenacious as the Realm's, in realty once you leave Lookshy's sphere of influence they are unlikely to pursue you much longer or further, whereas due to the Realm's status as the world power can, and will, challenge you wherever you try to hide in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T16:31:41-07:00","id":696609,"title":"","content":"Jesus, <i>outcastes</i> are going to get together to form Wyld Hunts, but Lookshy is going to settle for half-measures?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T16:52:17-07:00","id":696622,"title":"","content":"A group of Outcasts is hardly going to put their lives on hold for months or years in order to chase an Anathema across Creation. Once an Anathema leaves their territory, most of the time they will just say, &quot;Mission accomplished,&quot; and leave it at that. They have lives to live, families to take care of, jobs to perform, kingdoms to run, etc. And most of the time they aren't going to drop everything to chase down Anathema foe thousands of miles when it's clear he has no intention of sticking around in their territory. They're people with lives, not video game enemies.<br /> <br /> It's why the Realm's Wild Hunt is in a different league. Many Wild Hunts recruit monks for a reason. Monks generally don't have lives or major obligations outside of their religious duties. They are much better positioned to drop everything at a moments notice and chase the Anathema to the far ends of Creation. But that what makes the Realm's Wyld Hunt an exception and more dangerous and tenacious than local or regional Wyld Hunts. You probably shouldn't assume that Outcasts Wyld Hunts have the same scope as the Realm's Wild Hunts.<br /> <br /> If some Anathema is causing problems in the Scavenger Lands and he escapes from a Lookshyan Wild Hunt into the Linnowan lands and then keeps going North, it's very possible that the Lookshayan Wild Hunt will disengage and cease pursuit. Lookshy just doesn't typically have the manpower to spare on sending Wild Hunts across Creation in the same way that the Realm does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T17:18:12-07:00","id":696627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/689173-exigents-great-forks?p=696609#post696609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jesus, <i>outcastes</i> are going to get together to form Wyld Hunts, but Lookshy is going to settle for half-measures?</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of got the sense that a lot of outcaste &quot;Wyld Hunts&quot; are somewhat more impromptu and slapdash than the ones backed by a government of Terrestrials, but otherwise yeah...I don't see Lookshy half-assing things any more than their budget and limited sphere of influence compared to the Realm demands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T18:41:01-07:00","id":696711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/689173-exigents-great-forks?p=696622#post696622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A group of Outcasts is hardly going to put their lives on hold for months or years in order to chase an Anathema across Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>If he did something to merit them forming a Wyld Hunt, they will!<br /> <br /> Also, Wyld Hunt. With a &quot;y.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/689173-exigents-great-forks?p=696622#post696622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once an Anathema leaves their territory, most of the time they will just say, &quot;Mission accomplished,&quot; and leave it at that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't consider myself a vengeful person, but if you draw your sword and attack me, you'd better kill me with it, because just &quot;driving me off&quot; is going to <b>guarantee</b> this won't be the end of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T18:53:24-07:00","id":696729,"title":"","content":"If people who see themselves as humanity's lords and protectors find a demon whose very presence ushers in corruption, they'd probably feel like real assholes if they (1) underestimated the demon and let it flee to continue its wickedness and (2) responded to this failure by shrugging and going home. Not a lot of high fives right there.<br /> <br /> It's also probably not too often that a Solar gives up so easily. Why was he even found? If he turns on the light show, there's a scent chance he was trying to do something important, not just flaring his anima to impress the locals. Them Anathema are stubborn, so maybe don't let one get away!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T19:24:06-07:00","id":696738,"title":"","content":"While in theory the Dragon Blooded are kindred whom are unceasingly devoted to hunting down and killing the Anathema wherever they are found, the reality is probably a bit different. For most Dragon Blooded, facing off against one of the Anathema is likely going to be the most dangerous thing that Dragon Blooded ever does in his entire life. If they faced an Anathema, and the Anathema managed to survive and escape across a great distance, I can't imagine that most Dragon Blooded are so fanatical that they would willingly sacrifice their own lives, leaving their territories undefended and their families unprotected in order to chase an Anathema across Creation when that that Anathema no longer poses a realistic threat.<br /> <br /> The real threats to that Terrestrial's territory will be local Raksha, bandits, Realm incursions, etc, not some Anathema who buggered off to Coral. There is likely no shortage of stories in Creation about Dragon Blooded who spent years chasing some hated foe or wicked Anathema across Creation, only to eventually return home and find their family dead and everything they worked for in ruins.<br /> <br /> While non-Realm Dragon Blooded chasing an Anathema across Creation makes for a good setup for a chronicle, and reason for a group of Dragon Blooded to work together, it's generally going to be fairly unusual and atypical.<br /> <br /> Most Wyld Hunts probably end when an Anathema is dead or fled to the point that chasing them down is no longer realistic, and the Wyld Hunt is called off with the understanding that wherever that Anathema goes, a new Wild Hunt will be formed and track him down. He will be killed eventually. It will be the rare Wyld Hunt (likely fueled by a desire for revenge against that particular Anathema) in which the Wyld Hunt roams far beyond the territorial boundaries of its members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T19:31:00-07:00","id":696740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CycloneJoker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/689173-exigents-great-forks?p=696627#post696627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I kind of got the sense that a lot of outcaste &quot;Wyld Hunts&quot; are somewhat more impromptu and slapdash than the ones backed by a government of Terrestrials, but otherwise yeah...I don't see Lookshy half-assing things any more than their budget and limited sphere of influence compared to the Realm demands.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not half assing it. At worst it's being a bit short sighted, like how farmers were about properties starting on fire back in the Gay 90s. If it wasn't their land it wasn't their problem.<br /> <br /> And then the Great Hinckley Fire happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T20:53:49-07:00","id":696764,"title":"","content":"I hope that's some Outcastes, not all of them. I hope there are significant portions of Creation and even societies with Outcastes in them that don't believe in the Immaculate doctrine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T22:00:53-07:00","id":696773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/689173-exigents-great-forks?p=696738#post696738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While in theory the Dragon Blooded are kindred whom are unceasingly devoted to hunting down and killing the Anathema wherever they are found, the reality is probably a bit different. For most Dragon Blooded, facing off against one of the Anathema is likely going to be the most dangerous thing that Dragon Blooded ever does in his entire life. If they faced an Anathema, and the Anathema managed to survive and escape across a great distance, I can't imagine that most Dragon Blooded are so fanatical that they would willingly sacrifice their own lives, leaving their territories undefended and their families unprotected in order to chase an Anathema across Creation when that that Anathema no longer poses a realistic threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, if I found a demon in my kitchen and just barely managed to banish him to North Korea with my kitchen knife, I'm not going after him. I know there's innocent people there but god damn they need to take care of themselves and I've got other things to worry about.<br /> <br /> On the other hand most Solars probably aren't taken to simply leaving their home, they're chosen heroes of the rising sun! Especially if it's only an outcast Wyld Hunt, which are way more ragtag and unsupported.<br /> <br /> On the other other hand, I'm with Erinys I'd like to think that most outcastes out there probably only form Wyld Hunts when it's a Wyld invasion or there's a Solar/Lunar actively being a dick. If you're not part of a super zealous faith &quot;go try and kill that pants shittingly powerful dude over there because it's what a dynast would do.&quot; Probably isn't a good reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T22:07:36-07:00","id":696776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/689173-exigents-great-forks?p=695907#post695907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't imagine Lookshyan Dragon-Blooded had enough freedom to go off on personal glory-hunting adventures like that. Aren't they universally career military?</div> </div> </div> </div> Not quite; it's just the most prestigious career. While all Lookshyan Dragon-Blooded are socially and legally considered to be in active service even when they technically aren't, and are thus expected to answer a call to service on need, they actually aren't all on active military duty all of the time. They can follow non-military careers over the course of their long lives; and some do only do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T22:17:54-07:00","id":696777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/689173-exigents-great-forks?p=696773#post696773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand most Solars probably aren't taken to simply leaving their home, they're chosen heroes of the rising sun! Especially if it's only an outcast Wyld Hunt, which are way more ragtag and unsupported.</div> </div> </div> </div> Indeed, I don't imagine a lot of Celestials will just run away (they might run away from the Hunt, but probably only to strike back later).<br /> Some will. But one issue is that when a Celestial runs away, it may well be to hide. Consider, for example, if you attack a Lunar and she uses Travel Without Distance. Where's she gone? No idea. You stay in the area for 3 weeks, and she doesn't reappear. Did she take the form of a peasant and is just living a normal life? Is she watching you as a literal fly on the wall? Did she turn into an albatross and fly off to Coral? Did she go to the Wyld? No idea. So, you look for her for a while, but without leads, you may as well go home. If she turns up again, you'll have to go back and try something else, if she doesn't, well, congratulate yourselves and driving her off and stopping her evil plans.<br /> <br /> (This is another thing that less fanatical Dragonblood probably consider: the purpose of killing Anathema isn't actually killing Anathema. You can't kill them, all you can do is kill their current host, they'll just find another one somewhere. But what you can do is stop them building a power base, stop them training and developing their powers, and keep them running and scared. At the end of the day, the Anathema aren't a threat that can be defeated, merely one that can be kept down. Like plague, or ill-health. So, while killing them is best, ruining their plans, smashing their armies, and forcing them to flee to the wilderness to live like a dog is a solid second-best)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T02:52:55-07:00","id":696901,"title":"","content":"You know who else chased someone away after blatantly murdering someone close to him, telling him never to return, and setting his hounds after the guy just to be safe?<br /> <br /> Scar.<br /> <br /> Look how <i>that</i> turned out for him.<br /> <br /> (I'll admit, if the Anathema <i>escapes</i>, that's one thing, but you don't draw your sword with the intent of just chasing someone away.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-11-2015, 05:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T05:21:56-07:00","id":698508,"title":"","content":"I don't imagine Lookshy or anyone else half-ass'ing a Wyld Hunt. Their version of the Immaculate faith does still believe that Celestials are Anathema. <br /> <br /> What will get in their way is the territory of the other nations in the Scavenger Lands. Nexus isn't going to just let a Wyld Hunt composed of Lookshyan military traipse through their sovereign territory. Great Forks will feel much the same way, and so on.<br /> <br /> If we are looking for ambiguity and intrigue in the River Province, that's where you can find it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T09:40:46-07:00","id":702248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/689173-exigents-great-forks?p=696901#post696901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know who else chased someone away after blatantly murdering someone close to him, telling him never to return, and setting his hounds after the guy just to be safe?<br /> <br /> Scar.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I still say that telling a <i>child</i> that they're solely responsible for their parent's death (the *look* on Simba's face...) and telling them that they have no choice but to run away from home or they'll be killed for it, is still one of THE most bone-chillingly <i>evil</i> acts I have ever seen a Disney villain perform. To make matters even worse, he immediately sends his hyenas to murder Simba, indicating that he never intended him to live, so <i>he did all that just for the sheer fun of it.</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T09:48:26-07:00","id":702251,"title":"","content":"While on the subject of Great Forks, I had this idea (inspired by an anime, I'll admit!) about how God-Blooded youths in the city were forming street gangs and battling each other in turf wars. This was to be a symptom of the social unrest that set in after the loss of the city's troops; without those troops to keep youngsters in line, they are running amok. Also, they saw an entire generation of their elders die, arguably for nothing, and they don't want to throw their own lives away, so there's an element of rebellion against the established social order there, too. Instead of joining the states' army, they are forming their own, but multiple districts all have similar ideas, and now they're butting heads.<br /> <br /> So far, there have been only a few incidents of open violence, a couple of which disrupted the festivals and parades the city is so well-known for. The Gods whose services were disrupted have complained to the Three, but so far no action has been taken. The city waits, quiet but tense, to see what will happen next...<br /> <br /> I dunno, does this sound like it would be a good story for Great Forks?How might a heavy Exigent presence affect this set up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}